<title>USA: U.S. base metals and scrap prices - April 30.</title>
<headline>U.S. base metals and scrap prices - April 30.</headline>
<text>
<p>U.S. premiums added to LME official cash settlement price, except for copper, which is added to the COMEX spot month. Premium includes price for delivery to consumer's works.</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum: Western grade		    5.50-6.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Zinc: Special high grade SHG	     5.00.5.75 cents/pound</p>
<p>Lead					     2.00-2.25 cents/pound</p>
<p>Tin   (Grade A)				6.80-8.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>	(low lead, 50 ppm)		   8.10-9.50 cents/pound</p>
<p>Nickel (melting grade)		    9.00-10.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Copper (high grade cathode)		2.75-3.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum alloy (A380 grade), Midwest and East coast, delivered to consumer 75.00-76.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum scrap, Midwest and East coast average price,</p>
<p>delivered to consumer</p>
<p>Old Sheet and Cast metal	     52 to 54     cents/pound</p>
<p>Turnings, clean and dry		53 to 54     cents/pound</p>
